{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-27T07:42:04.537Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Both the task verify and the proposal verify (`pnpm verify`) pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `osq inbox` and its ordered dispatch view in the task's scope:\n\n- **`src/core/status/dispatch.ts`** (new) — composes `readDispatchItems` → `orderDispatchItems` → `readDispatchCard`. `readDispatch` reads only the first item's card (text), `readDispatchQueue` reads every card (JSON).\n- **`src/core/status/dispatch-text.ts`** (new) — `formatDispatchText` prints `Nothing needs you.` or `Needs you (<n>):`, one line per item, a blank line, then the first card (`<kind>: <folder>`, `why:`, kind body, `Actions:`). The approval body is `formatApprovalDigest`'s output.\n- **`src/cli/inbox-dispatch.ts`** (new) — `inboxDispatchCommand` (stdout-injectable) and `registerInboxDispatchCommand` for `osq inbox [--json]`.\n- **`src/cli/index.ts`** — registers it beside `registerMessageCommand`; now 246 lines (under 250).\n- **`README.md`** — Commands list and Human Attention Inbox section document `osq inbox` and its ordering.\n- **`tests/inbox-dispatch.test.ts`** (new) — covers all four \"Inbox dispatch command\" scenarios plus card evidence.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/097-inbox-dispatch-order/.run/results/4.md`.\n\nTouched: src/core/status/dispatch.ts, src/core/status/dispatch-text.ts, src/cli/inbox-dispatch.ts, src/cli/index.ts, README.md, tests/inbox-dispatch.test.ts"}}
